\section{Routines description}
The model used in the fit is the single resonance reflection coeficinent of Eq.~\ref{S11}
considering a constant attenuation $\alpha$:
\begin{equation}
\left|S_{11}\right|=\alpha
\sqrt{\frac{(\beta-1)^2+(Q_0 \delta)^2}{(\beta+1)^2+(Q_0 \delta)^2}}.
\quad \mbox{with} \quad
\alpha \in [0,1].
\label{S11alpha}
\end{equation}

As an estimation of the quality of the fit, we could quadratically sum the difference between
the  data $\widetilde{S_{11}}$ and its estimation $S_{11}$, i.e.
\begin{equation}
\sigma_{||}=
\sqrt{\frac{\sum \left(\left|S_{11}\right|-\left|\widetilde{S_{11}}\right| \right)^2}{N-N_{par}}}
\quad \mbox{and} \quad
\sigma_{\angle}=
\sqrt{\frac{\sum \left(\angle S_{11} -\angle \widetilde{S_{11}} \right)^2 }{N-N_{par}}},
\end{equation}
where the sum is weighted for the number of effective degree of freedoms that is the difference
between the number of data points and the number of fit parameters $N_{par}$.


\begin{itemize}
\item
Interpolation from Eq.~\ref{S11alpha} keeping $f_0$, $\beta$, $Q_0$ as free parameters of the
fit. The attenuation $\alpha$ is given. Results in the following figures are drawn with 
magenta lines.
\\ {\bf MATLAB routine}: S11fit.m.
\item
Interpolation from Eq.~\ref{S11alpha} keeping $\beta$, $Q_0$ as free parameters of the
fit. The resonance frequency is chosen as the minimum of the $\left|S_{11}\right|$ and its
unceratinty as the frequency sample separation divided by $\sqrt{12}$. The attenuation $\alpha$
is given.  Results in the following figures are drawn with 
blue lines.
\\ {\bf MATLAB routine}: S11fit\_delta.m.
\item
Interpolation from Eq.~\ref{S11alpha} keeping $\beta$, $Q_0$ and $\alpha$ as free parameters of the
fit. The resonance frequency is chosen as the minimum of the $\left|S_{11}\right|$ and its
unceratinty as the frequency sample separation divided by $\sqrt{12}$. Results in the following
figures are drawn with green lines. 
\\ {\bf MATLAB routine}: S11fit\_delta\_attentation.m.
\item
Interpolation from Eq.~\ref{S11alpha} keeping $f_0$, $\beta$, $Q_0$ and $\alpha$ as free
parameters of the 
fit. Results in the following
figures are drawn with black lines. 
\\ {\bf MATLAB routine}: S11fit\_attentation.m.
\end{itemize}


